    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Guardians' Curse",
      "actions": 2,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "curse",
        "divine",
        "misfortune"
      ],
      "text": "Frequency three times per day\n\n---\nEffect The guardian flock bestows a curse upon all enemies in a 5-foot emanation by touching them with their scythes. Each affected creature must attempt a DC 33 Will save save.\n\n---\nCritical Success The target is unaffected and is temporarily immune to Guardians' Curse for 24 hours.\n\nSuccess The target feels a momentary shudder of doom and is Stupefied 1 for 1 minute by the distracting sensation.\n\nFailure The target becomes morose and glum as it accepts its own inevitable fate. For 1 hour, the target is Stupefied 2. Each time the target gains the dying condition, the stupefied condition value increases by 1, to a maximum value of Stupefied 4.\n\nCritical Failure As failure, but the effect is permanent.",
      "frequency": {
        "max": 3,
        "per": "day"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Harvest the Wicked",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "1 to 3\n\nFrequency once per round\n\n---\nEffect The vanths swing their scythes in a coordinated melee attack. Each enemy in a 5-foot emanation must attempt a DC 30 basic Reflex save save. The damage depends on the number of actions. The slashing damage is treated as adamantine, cold iron, and silver.\n\n1 1d10+1 slashing damage plus 1d6 shepherd's touch\n\n2 2d10+3 slashing damage plus 3d6 shepherd's touch\n\n3 2d10+7 slashing damage plus 4d6 shepherd's touch",
      "frequency": {
        "max": 1,
        "per": "round"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Shepherd's Touch",
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "The physical damage dealt by the guardian flock's Harvest the Wicked ability is treated as coming from a weapon with a ghost touch property rune. In addition, the vanths deal the listed damage as void damage to living creatures or vitality damage to undead.",
      "rules": [
